chapter.v:
	My son, 

	 if you become surety for your friend,If you have shaken hands in pledge for a stranger,
 [Jer. 40:8, 13;]

	A worthless 

	 person, a wicked man,Walks with a perverse mouth;
 [Neh. 1:11; Ps. 106:46; Prov. 16:7]

	He winks 

	 with his eyes,He shuffles his feet,He points with his fingers;
 [Jer. 44:16]
